# Local Netlify folder
.netlify/*
!.netlify/functions-serve/
.netlify/functions-serve/*
!.netlify/functions-serve/package.json

# Same thing anywhere under src/, at any depth. A pattern containing a slash is anchored
# to the directory holding this .gitignore, so the rules above only ever matched a
# top-level .netlify/ — which is how two nested CLI trees ended up tracked:
# src/.netlify/ (144 files, ~80 MB) and src/netlify/functions/.netlify/ (443 files,
# ~24 MB). The `**` matches zero or more directories, so this covers both and any future
# one. Everything in them is Netlify CLI state; netlify.toml points at
# src/netlify/functions (no dot) for real source.
src/**/.netlify/
node_modules
blog/_site/
blog-built/
blog/.jekyll-cache/
blog/.jekyll-metadata
.env
assets/videos/
old/
scratch_notes.txt
notes.txt
users/
